.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.cursor/

# .claude holds both personal state and shared project config. Ignore it at
# every depth, then re-admit exactly two files at the repo root: the Rams
# design-review hook and the settings that wire it up. settings.local.json
# (personal permissions) and any nested .claude stay ignored.
#
# The leading slashes matter. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to this
# file's directory, so bare `.claude/*` would only ever match the root one and
# would quietly un-ignore ai-hedge-fund/.claude. `**/.claude/` catches all
# depths; the `!/` lines then carve out the root exceptions. Re-including a
# file also requires re-including its directory first, which is what `!/.claude/`
# is doing before `/.claude/*` re-excludes the contents.
**/.claude/
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.vite/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
ai-hedge-fund/.gstack/
.gstack/
